# F-01 correction baseline (planner-owned, additive)
#
# Prepared 2026-10-02 after docs/reviews/F-01.md returned CHANGES_REQUIRED.
#
# Revision history (both revisions happened BEFORE any implementer started, so no
# implementer ever received a superseded draft):
#   rev 1 - first correction suite draft. Superseded, never handed over.
#   rev 2 - corrected an R3 assertion that inserted an unassociated post (which
#           would have fought the correct posts.gate_id NOT NULL fix) and replaced
#           an unsafe RegExp object-matcher with a strict SQLSTATE assertion.
#           See the addendum in docs/handoffs/F-01-corrections-prepared.md.
#   rev 3 - current. docs/reviews/F-01-correction-preparation.md found the
#           normalised-lookup query normalised the literal $1 instead of the
#           table column and was not a bound query, and found the suite was not
#           self-contained. The lookup now compares the canonicalised table column
#           against a canonicalised, properly bound parameter, every diagnostic
#           mutation runs in its own rolled-back transaction, and the RED evidence
#           distinguishes accepted-invalid-data failures from missing-column
#           failures. See docs/handoffs/F-01-corrections-prepared.md.
#   rev 4 - current. docs/reviews/F-01-correction-followup.md required an isolated
#           unclaimed-gate location-consistency case, an explicit cardinality
#           decision (many posts per gate, NOT one-post-per-gate), a real
#           legacy-0002 upgrade test refusing an ambiguous mapping, and a corrected
#           mutation interpretation that does not demand a redundant constraint fail
#           independently. Adds f01-legacy-upgrade.test.ts. See Addendum 3.
#
# This file is ADDITIVE: docs/handoffs/F-01-tests.sha256 and its 14 entries remain
# authoritative and byte-identical, as do all original acceptance assertions.
# Verify BOTH manifests before implementing and before reviewing.
#   rev 5 - current. docs/reviews/F-01-latest-correction-review.md required a
#           positive legacy shared-gate upgrade case and a repair of the complete
#           migration path. Planner-approved compatibility amendment (Addendum 4):
#           0003 drops the never-approved posts_gate_id_unique statement;
#           0005 becomes DROP CONSTRAINT IF EXISTS. Pre-amendment hashes:
#             90de4cdced192d0386a5f3b533b3b7795c8b28151976978a47541120576f5a58  0003
#             0e39b800a9bfb6eb835869e6be6172d94da1e577cea1af20c8daecd5f0707bf0  0005
#           Already-applied databases are unaffected: drizzle selects pending
#           migrations by folderMillis, not content hash, so the ledger retains the
#           pre-amendment hashes as the audit trail of this amendment.
